{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"field of regard field of regard","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md","fileName":"Field of Regard.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Field of Regard","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Perception and Navigation]] [[XR Environments]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","XR Environments","Visual Display","Field of View","Head-Worn Display","Display Fidelity","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"field of regard field of regard","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Field of Regard.md","fileName":"Field of Regard.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Field of Regard","heading":"Field of Regard","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Field of regard is the amount of physical space around a user in which a [[Visual Display]] can present imagery. It is measured in degrees of visual angle.\n\nIt differs from [[Field of View]], which is the portion visible at a single instant. A cylindrical display may offer a 360-degree horizontal field of regard. A tracked [[Head-Worn Display]] can also provide a 360-degree field of regard because the display remains in front of the eyes as the user turns, even when its instantaneous field of view is much smaller.\n\nField of regard is one component of [[Display Fidelity]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","XR Environments","Visual Display","Field of View","Head-Worn Display","Display Fidelity","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,